3. Handling multiple threads safely is a complex task in C that requires careful synchronization mechanisms (like mutexes) or thread-specific data structures.
4. In general, cryptographic functions are low-level and often require deep understanding of the specific algorithm to use correctly. It would be best to abstract these details behind a higher-level interface, so as not to complicate things for developers who want to use them. 
