2. There are no thread safety measures in place, which means that if two threads were trying to use this with the same password at the same time, one could overwrite another's key/IV causing a security issue. 
3. The KDF used is PBKDF2 with SHA-1, which has been shown to have vulnerabilities. This code uses SHA-1 for demonstration purposes only. For actual use, you should use a more secure hash function like SHA-256 or even better, one of the SHA-3 families.
