This function works by using the `std::find` algorithm to search for the first occurrence of the target string in the vector. If it is found, it replaces it with the replacement string. Otherwise, it inserts the target string at the beginning of the vector. This approach ensures that we don't have to traverse the entire vector if the target string is not found in the first few elements, which could improve performance for large vectors.
